{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the young man ran, etc.</b> One needs to know why the teller was agitated to report that they prophesied. And further, that he was agitated about them to put them in prison — is everyone who prophesies punished for prophesying? This is astonishing. Now, one may give a reason for the view of the one who says that they were two who remained among the written ones, for since Moshe said to Israel by the word of HaShem that He would place a spirit of prophecy upon seventy, and now these two also prophesied, there is reason to fear one of two things: either Moshe would not believe, Heaven forbid, in the statement that HaShem had told him seventy, or the prophesiers prophesied falsely. And according to the view of the one who says they were among the seventy, they reported to Moshe the improper deed — for he had said that they should go to the Tent of Meeting, and they stood in the camp and prophesied there — and in this there are two evils: one, that they did not fulfill the word of Moshe; and the second, that in this they revealed their mind, that they did not want the spirit to be bestowed upon them from the spirit of Moshe but rather from the source of the spirit, and they prophesied in the camp."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:51.694755449Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}